From f30d69b87b9d1f25f7e3c12aa35f729b33368a47 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Barnes <hello@jonbarnes.dev>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 22:56:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] The ray tracing shader cache and resources, as the smallest
 thing that compiles

Patch 0002 of the renderer series (OoT: Recompiled, .scaffold/upgrades/lighting-design.md).

rt64_framebuffer_renderer.h, rt64_application.h, rt64_workload_queue.h and
rt64_shared_queue_resources.h include render/rt64_raytracing_shader_cache.h and
render/rt64_raytracing_resources.h under RT_ENABLED, and the tree holds neither, so the path
named RaytracingShaderCache, RaytracingResources, RaytracingScene, RaytracingState,
RaytracingConfiguration, RaytracingShaderPrograms and UberShaderHash without defining them.

This patch writes both headers and their sources with every member the renderer touches,
declared with the type the renderer expects, and every method a no-op that creates nothing: no
texture, buffer, view, descriptor set, pipeline or acceleration structure exists until a later
patch makes one. It adds the blue noise generator patch 0001 pointed the application at (a
placeholder table until the shadow pass in phase 54 brings a real one). With the level Off the
renderer reaches none of this past construction and updateMultisampling(), so Off stays byte
identical to the baseline; the proof is tools/texture_compare.py against the phase 51 captures.

